From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ricardo Pardini <ricardo@pardini.net>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:52:58 +0100
Subject: media: cec: add MediaTek MT8195 HDMI CEC driver

Add a driver for the HDMI CEC controller of the MediaTek MT8195. It is
a separate block from the HDMI transmitter, with its own registers,
interrupt and clocks. The driver registers a standalone CEC adapter and
gets the physical address from the HDMI transmitter through the CEC
notifier.

The hardware ACKs messages addressed to its logical address by itself.
It has three logical address slots; the driver uses one.

The hardware does not wait for the signal free time before it starts a
new message on an idle bus. The driver therefore delays the start of a
transmit until the bus has been free for the signal free time given by
the CEC core. Hardware retransmissions are disabled, and the CEC core
does the retries.

The CEC block does not depend on the hotplug detect signal of the HDMI
transmitter, so CEC_CAP_NEEDS_HPD is not set.

The hardware programming is based on the MediaTek vendor driver by
Tommy Chen.

Co-developed-by: Tommy Chen <tommyyl.chen@mediatek.com>
Signed-off-by: Tommy Chen <tommyyl.chen@mediatek.com>
